---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../../components/ProjectCard.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Work"
  description="Case studies and selected projects by Eric Nolan across AI engineering, developer tooling, practical software, and product design."
>
  <header class="subhero subhero--work">
    <div class="shell subhero-grid">
      <div class="subhero-copy">
        <div class="subhero-badges">
          <span>AI ENGINEERING</span>
          <span>PRODUCT SYSTEMS</span>
          <span>PUBLIC EVIDENCE</span>
        </div>
        <p class="subhero-kicker">WORK // BUILD LOG</p>
        <h1>Proof beats positioning.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          The portfolio is deliberately mixed: AI infrastructure, developer tooling, private workflow products, live telemetry, and research. I want the systems to show how I think—not just the titles on my résumé.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-pop" href="#featured">Jump to the evidence ↓</a>
          <a class="button secondary case-secondary" href="https://github.com/unyieldingclaw-dev">Open GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="work-console" aria-label="Portfolio snapshot">
        <div class="work-console__top">
          <span>PORTFOLIO STATUS</span>
          <i></i>
        </div>
        <div class="work-console__metric">
          <strong>AI</strong>
          <span>Context · agents · governance · verification</span>
        </div>
        <div class="work-console__metric">
          <strong>PRODUCT</strong>
          <span>Travel · whiskey · bowling · BBQ telemetry</span>
        </div>
        <div class="work-console__metric">
          <strong class="egg-inline" data-egg="Apparently 'leave it alone' is not a supported operating mode." data-trail-hover="work-console">MODE</strong>
          <span>Build it · use it · harden it · document it</span>
        </div>
        <div class="work-console__footer">
          <span>OPEN SOURCE + PUBLIC-SAFE PRIVATE CASE STUDIES</span>
        </div>
        <button class="trail-marker trail-marker--console" type="button" data-trail-marker="work-buildlog" aria-label="Hidden trail marker: Build Log">◇</button>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section section--projects" id="featured">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--punch">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Featured case studies</p>
          <h2>Different problems. Same operating style.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Understand the workflow. Model the real constraints. Automate only what earns automation. Make failure visible. Ship something people can actually use.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-grid project-grid--work-misaligned">
        <ProjectCard
          title="Personal Memory Bank"
          href="/work/personal-memory-bank/"
          eyebrow="AI engineering · Context systems"
          description="Persistent project memory governed by authority, freshness, provenance, hooks, diagnostics, semantic drift detection, review workflows, and CI."
          status="Open source"
          tags={['Context', 'Governance', 'CLI', 'Developer productivity']}
          tone="blue"
        />
        <ProjectCard
          title="AI Code Review Agent"
          href="/work/ai-code-review-agent/"
          eyebrow="Developer tooling · Local AI"
          description="Local multi-agent review with specialist isolation, sanitized diffs, confidence-aware findings, privacy-conscious inference, and multiple developer interfaces."
          status="Open source"
          tags={['Ollama', 'Agents', 'Security', 'Verification']}
          tone="emerald"
        />
        <ProjectCard
          title="Side Quest Atlas"
          href="/work/side-quest-atlas/"
          eyebrow="Travel memory product"
          description="Private small-group travel memory capture designed around 'capture now, enrich later,' group ownership, and clear access boundaries."
          status="Private case study"
          tags={['Flutter', 'Supabase', 'RLS', 'Product modeling']}
          tone="gold"
        />
        <ProjectCard
          title="PitLogic"
          href="/work/pitlogic/"
          eyebrow="Telemetry product"
          description="Client-side BBQ telemetry and analytics with live device integration, alerts, stall detection, forecasting, history, and data portability."
          status="Open source"
          tags={['React', 'PWA', 'Telemetry', 'Analytics']}
          tone="copper"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--private-lab">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Private, not hidden</p>
          <h2>Privacy can be a product decision too.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-intro">
          A private repository is not a weak portfolio artifact when the product contains family history, club data, or personal performance records. The case study exposes the judgment without exposing the people.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-grid project-grid--work-misaligned project-grid--work-private">
        <ProjectCard
          title="Tipsy Bunghole"
          href="/work/tipsy-bunghole/"
          eyebrow="Live event workflow"
          description="A private whiskey-club product that coordinates blind tasting events across participant, steward, and host roles while preserving institutional memory."
          status="Private case study"
          tags={['React', 'Supabase', 'Roles', 'Event state']}
          tone="copper"
        />
        <ProjectCard
          title="Bowling Tracker"
          href="/work/bowling-tracker/"
          eyebrow="Sports tracking"
          description="A focused bowling product for sessions, scoring, equipment, patterns, leagues, drills, and analytics—designed around the bowler's actual workflow."
          status="Private case study"
          tags={['Flutter', 'Offline sync', 'Analytics', 'Domain rules']}
          tone="slate"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark work-bridge">
    <div class="shell bridge-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The research underneath it</p>
        <h2>Harness Engineering</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Building PMB and ACR kept exposing the same truth: model quality is only one variable. Context, tools, state, authority, evaluation, and execution boundaries decide whether the whole system is trustworthy.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="bridge-card" href="/harness-engineering/">
        <span>ENTER THE FRAMEWORK</span>
        <strong>Context → Tools → Orchestration → Governance → Verification</strong>
        <small>Explore the systems around the model →</small>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
